// Two Windows bodies, each broken in a DIFFERENT pass. On any other target both
// are discarded before resolution, so neither error may surface.
//
// Two and not one, because they hide each other: resolution runs first, so a
// body carrying both errors reports only the R2006 and the type error goes
// unpinned. Split across two declarations, Windows reports both.
//
// The R2006 half was the untested one. The SPEC says a non-matching body is
// "never resolved AND never type-checked", and a fixture carrying only a type
// error left the resolution half resting on nothing: move selection to AFTER
// name resolution and the type error stays hidden, while this catches it.

module "main"

@target(.Windows)
platform_tag :: fn() -> string = 42

@target(.Windows)
platform_kind :: fn() -> string = no_such_function_anywhere()
